! ax5b_160_test1ab_mask.strap -- jb_ax5b "I-BOX 5", routine 1260
! ("----1260---CHECK MASK, INDICATOR, AND INTERRUPT.", banner PDF p.8),
! its prologue and TESTs 1A and 1B, IBM's own test of the MASK
! REGISTER's fixed bits:
!
!   PDF p.8    014064.00-014066.40  I60: the prologue (SSIP's IDF1)
!   PDF p.8    014067.00            I60ID: location printed, NO code
!   PDF p.9    014070.00-014112.40  I601: TEST 1A, the bit-24 guard,
!                                   its abort path, and the bit loop
!   PDF pp.9-11  014113.00-014162.40  I60B1: TEST 1A's error table,
!                                   bits 00-19, four half-words each
!   PDF p.11   014163.00-014166.40  I606: exit (B,SSW), continuity BIT0
!   PDF p.12   014167.00-014207.00  I607: TEST 1B
!   PDF pp.12-13  014207.40-014247.00  I60B2: TEST 1B's error table,
!                                   bits 48-63
!   PDF p.13   014247.40-014253.00  I6010: exit (B,SSW), continuity BIT1
!   PDF p.114  024501.00-024552.00  the constant pool and BIT0-BIT24, as
!                                   decks/ax5b_bit_table.strap transcribes
!                                   them (verified there, row by row)
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi, and 014111.40 again
! at 400 dpi (its "0D" looks like "00" at 150).  Checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax5b_160_test1ab_mask_listing.py (240 rows, 18 symbols).
!
! THE BANNER'S OWN WORDS FOR TEST 1 (p.8, verbatim):
!         -TEST 1 CHECKS THAT THE PROGRAMMABLE
!              -BITS OF THE MASK REGISTER CAN
!              -BE SET TO BOTH ONE AND ZERO,
!              -THAT BITS 0-19 ARE ONE, AND
!              -THAT BITS 48-63 ARE ZERO.
! TEST 1C (I6011, pp.14-21, "CHECK THAT BITS 20-47 OF MASK REG CAN BE
! SET TO 1 OR 0") is the programmable half and is NOT in this deck.
!
! WHAT THE RULE IS.  Reference Manual Figure 11, the Indicator List
! (printed p.43, PDF p.46), read in the page image: its "Mask" column
! prints 1 for indicators 0-19, "m" (settable) for 20-47 and 0 for
! 48-63.  The mask register is word 12 (TI,1,0,12.0 prints its second
! address as 000014.02, octal 14).  The model has the rule in
! bsv/StretchStorage.bsv (the addrMask write and the register's reset
! value).  Other ax5b decks write the mask (Z,$MASK; TI into $MASK)
! but none checks its FIXED bits, and StretchStorage.bsv's own comment
! records that the model once forced only 0-15, not 0-19, and that no
! test caught it.  This is IBM's test of exactly those bits.
!
! HOW TEST 1A WORKS (all from the Reference Manual, printed pp.24-25,
! PDF pp.27-28, and the printed code):
!   * LX,$X0,I00Z / SX,$X0,12.0 and TI,1,0,12.0 zero every settable
!     bit; TI,1,12.0,$X0 reads the mask back into X0.  KV,$X0,BIT24
!     (p.24: "The address part, bits 0-24, of the half-word ... is
!     compared with the address part, bits 0-24, of the index word ...
!     Comparison is algebraic") compares against BIT24, which is -0:
!     X0 is +(bits 0-19 ones) unless mask bit 24 is stuck on, which
!     makes X0 negative.  BXH is the pass path.  On failure the block
!     credits continuity BIT0, BIT1 and BIT2 at once and jumps to TEST 2
!     (I6041) -- "UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS".
!   * The loop runs twenty times (LCI,$X2,20).  Pass k: X1 = mask word
!     (TI), then V+,$X1,BIT(k-1) (BIT0-1.0, the zeroed word 024521.00,
!     on pass 0), then KV,$X1,BITk; BZXL (not low) is the pass path.
!     When bits 0..k-1 are all one, adding bit k-1 carries out through
!     bit 0 and is lost (p.24: "The overflow which may occur in index
!     arithmetic is ignored"), leaving bits k-19: not low against BITk
!     exactly when bit k is one.  A failure falls into I604's "$B,0",
!     whose address SVA set to the k-th entry of I60B1.
!   * The addresses step by self-modification: LV,$X2,I603+.32 loads
!     the KV half-word itself as a signed value, and its bit 24 -- the
!     first bit of the KV op code (hex 90) -- is ONE, so the value is
!     negative and V-I,$X2,1.0 INCREASES its magnitude by a word.  That
!     is the printed comment "-SUB TO INCCREMENT, BIT 24 IS 2." (sic).
!     TEST 1B's I608 does the same ("-SUB TO INCREMENT, BIT 24 IS 1.0").
!
! HOW TEST 1B WORKS: sixteen passes (LCI,$X1,16).  Each loads all ones
! into the mask (LX,$X2,I00O / TI,1,$X2,12.0), reads it back into X2,
! then SR,$X2,$X2 stores X2's own refill field (mask bits 46-63) into
! bits 0-17 of X2's value and zeroes bits 18-24 (p.24, STORE REFILL).
! Mask bits 46-47 are settable, so they are ONE: the three-pass loop at
! I607A ("-DELETE ANY BITS IN 0 AND 1.") adds BIT1 until the value is
! not above BIT2, the carry out of bit 0 again being lost.  Then
! KV,$X2,<BIT3 + pass>; BXL (low) is the pass path, I609's "$B,0" the
! failure, into I60B2's entry for that pass.
!
! A LABELLING QUIRK OF IBM'S, traced from the code and NOT smoothed:
! after SR, mask bit 48+m sits in value bit 2+m, but the first
! comparand is BIT3, not BIT2.  Pass j fails when any of value bits
! 0..3+j is set, so a lone mask bit 48 or 49 both report at entry 0
! ("-BIT 48 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO."), and a lone mask bit k >= 49 reports
! at entry k-49, whose message names bit k-1.  The last pass (BIT18)
! compares a field SR has zeroed and can never fail.  The model
! injection M2 below confirms the shift: a leaking bit 55 lands in the
! "-BIT 54" entry.
!
! TWO SEGMENTS.  TEST 1A ends in its own "B,SSW" at 014164.40 and TEST
! 1B at 014251.00.  With SSW a PASS halt the suite runs the deck twice:
! from END (I60, the prologue, which falls into I601 through SSIP's
! IDF1) and with ENTRY=I607.  The continuity rows after each B,SSW, and
! TEST 1A's abort path, are transcribed and verified but never run.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: both segments PASS IBM's checks (PC 1410 = SSW,
! SEN 0).  No disagreement with the listing.
!   I60 (END: prologue, TEST 1A): RET (word 001306) = 0x60d8800, the
!     return to 014066.00; X0 = 0x61c400000000000, value 014161.00 =
!     I60B1 + 19 entries (the 20th pass exits before the step); X1 =
!     0x100000000000, value bit 19 alone = mask + BIT18 on the last
!     pass; X2 = 0xa59428000000000, value -(024545.02) (BIT19 with the
!     KV's J), count 0.  CYCLES 4107.
!   I607 (TEST 1B): X0 = 0x629600000000000, value 014245.40 = I60B2 +
!     15 entries; X1 = 0 (count spent); X2 = 0x7fffff0000: value 0
!     after the delete, and the mask's settable bits 25-47 still ones in
!     flag, spare, count and refill; X3 = 0xa59048000080000, value
!     -(024544.04) = BIT18 with the KV's J, count 2 (one delete pass).
!     CYCLES 5426.
!   X values print the model's packIndexWord layout (bsv/StretchTypes.bsv):
!   value in bits 63-40, sign 39, flag 38, spare 37-36, count 35-18,
!   refill 17-0.  CYCLES is MODEL BEHAVIOUR.
!
! MODEL INJECTIONS, OBSERVED (a scratch copy of bsv/, both runs repeated
! for each; the tracked bsv/ never touched):
!   M1 mask bit 7 (BSV 56) not forced to one on a write
!     ("20'hFEFFF" for "20'hFFFFF" in StretchStorage.bsv's addrMask
!     write) -> I60 FAIL: PC 1416 (SERS), SEN 0x616800000000000 (return
!     014132.00, i.e. the entry at 014131.00, "-BIT 07 OF MASK REG NOT
!     ONE."), X0 0x616400000000000 (014131.00 = I60B1 + 7 entries), X1
!     0xfff00000000000, X2 0xa56428000340000, CYCLES 1777.  I607 PASSES
!     with every pin.
!   M2 mask bit 55 (BSV 8) writable instead of always zero
!     ("{20'hFFFFF, v[43:16], 7'h0, v[8], 8'h00}") -> I607 FAIL: PC 1416,
!     SEN 0x625200000000000 (return 014224.40), X0 0x624e00000000000
!     (014223.40, the entry printed "-BIT 54 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO." --
!     the k-1 labelling above, observed), X1 0x280000 (count 10 left),
!     X2 0x40007fffff0100, X3 0xa56c48000080000, CYCLES 2376.  I60
!     PASSES with every pin (TEST 1A zeroes the settable bits first).
!   CONTROL: the unmodified bsv/ in the same scratch copy: both runs PASS
!     with the pins in run_tests.sh.  StretchStorage.bsv restored from a
!     saved copy between injections; cmp IDENTICAL at the end.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points at the addresses jb_ax4b PDF p.193's SYN table
!     prints, which these pages' own machine code repeats (SSW 1301.0,
!     SERS 1304.0, RET 1306.40, SEN 1310.0, SENO 1311.0, DPET13 1437.0,
!     IDF1 1443.0).  SSW is a PASS halt, SERS a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO data
!     words SIC stores into.  RET is a "$B,0" half-word whose address
!     field SIC,RET fills and IDF1 ("print ID") is a bare branch to it:
!     that return path is INFERRED, as in decks/ax4b_156_test1_lvs.strap,
!     from routine 148's own SIC/$B idiom; no SSIP page shows IDF1's
!     body.  DPET13 is a data word.  SIC "is executed if and only if the
!     associated branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed
!     p.41, PDF 44), so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the error entry
!     on a failure.
!   * IC260 (022737.00) and I6041 (014556.00) are SYN'd at the addresses
!     these pages' own machine code prints for them ("LX,$X13,IC260"
!     22737.32 10; "BD,16041" 14556.04 00).
!   * Notation only: "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")"; the label
!     glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I60.., I00O), as for
!     every ax5b label (docs/listing_typography.md).
!   * I60ID prints a location and no code, so it is SYN'd; the word
!     there is not in this image.
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1306.40
RET     $B, 0                         ! SUBSTITUTE: SSIP's return half-word
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
        SLC, (8)1437.0
DPET13  DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SSIP's ident cell
        SLC, (8)1443.0
IDF1    B, RET                        ! SUBSTITUTE: SSIP's "print ID"
!
! ---- routine 1260's own labels outside these pages, SYN'd at the
! addresses this listing prints for them (inputs, not witnesses) ------
IC260   SYN, (8)22737.0               ! -CONTINUITY REG 1260. (PDF p.83)
I6041   SYN, (8)14556.0               ! -TEST 2, CHK DATA IN IA. (PDF p.22)
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.8, 014064.00-014066.40: routine 1260's prologue
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)14064.0
I60     LX, $X1, I60ID                ! -UPDATE IDENT.
        SX, $X1, DPET13
        SIC, RET
        B, IDF1                       ! -PRINT ID.
        Z, IC260
        BD, I601
        CNOP
! I60ID  %IQSZ@DD%BU,64,8@,I260     Z        014067.00, no machine code
I60ID   SYN, (8)14067.0
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.9, 014070.00-014122.40: TEST 1A -- the bit-24 check, the loop,
! and the error table's entries for bits 00-03
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)14070.0
I601    LX, $X0, I00Z                 ! -TEST 1A, CHECK THAT BITS 0-19 OF
        SX, $X0, 12.0                 ! -MASK REGISTER ARE ALWAYS ONES.
        TI, 1, 0, 12.0
        TI, 1, 12.0, $X0
        KV, $X0, BIT24
        BXH, I602
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 24 OF MASK REG STUCK ON 1,UNABLE
        B, SERS                       ! -TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        LX, $X13, IC260               ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+, $X13, BIT0
        V+, $X13, BIT1
        V+, $X13, BIT2
        SX, $X13, IC260
        BD, I6041
!
I602    Z, BIT0-1.0                   ! -BITS 0-19.
        LVI, $X0, BIT0-1.0
        SVA, $X0, I603
        V+I, $X0, 1.00
        SVA, $X0, I603+.32
        LCI, $X2, 20
        LVI, $X0, I60B1
I605    SVA, $X0, I604
        TI, 1, 12.0, $X1
I603    V+, $X1, 0
        KV, $X1, 0
        BZXL, $+1.0
I604    $B, 0
!
        C-I, $X2, 1.0
        BXCZ, I606
        V+I, $X0, 2.0
        LV, $X2, I603+.32
        SVA, $X2, I603
        V-I, $X2, 1.0                 ! -SUB TO INCCREMENT, BIT 24 IS 2.
        SVA, $X2, I603+.32
        B, I605
!                                     -YOU CAME TO THIS ERROR TABLE FROM 1604
I60B1   SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 00 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 01 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 02 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 03 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
! ---- PDF p.10 ----
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 04 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 05 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 06 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 07 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 08 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 09 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 10 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 11 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 12 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 13 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
! ---- PDF p.11 ----
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 14 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 15 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 16 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 17 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 18 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 19 OF MASK REG NOT ONE.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I606
        NOP
!
I606    B, $+1.0
        BD, I601
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B, SSW
        BD, $+.32
        LX, $X13, IC260               ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+, $X13, BIT0
        SX, $X13, IC260
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.12, 014167.00-014221.40: TEST 1B; p.13, 014222.00-014253.00
! ======================================================================
I607    LVI, $X0, BIT3                ! -TEST 1B, CHECK THAT BITS 48-63 OF
        SVA, $X0, I608                ! -MASK REG ARE ALWAYS ZERO.
        LVI, $X0, I60B2
        SVA, $X0, I609
        LCI, $X1, 16
I607B   LX, $X2, I00O
        TI, 1, $X2, 12.0
        NOP
        NOP
        TI, 1, 12.0, $X2
        SR, $X2, $X2
        NOP
!
        LCI, $X3, 3.0                 ! -DELETE ANY BITS IN 0 AND 1.
I607A   KV, $X2, BIT2
        BZXH, I608
        V+, $X2, BIT1
        CB, $X3, I607A
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BITS 0 AND 1 OF IX 2 CANT BE
        B, SERS                       ! -FORCED TO 00 CONDITION.
        B, I6010                      ! -TERMINATE.
!
I608    KV, $X2, 0
        BXL, $+1.0
I609    $B, 0
!
        C-I, $X1, 1.0
        BXCZ, I6010
        LV, $X3, I608
        V-I, $X3, 1.0                 ! -SUB TO INCREMENT, BIT 24 IS 1.0
        SVA, $X3, I608
        V+I, $X0, 2.0
        SVA, $X0, I609
        B, I607B
!                                     -YOU CAME TO THIS ERROR TABLE FROM 1609
I60B2   SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 48 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I6010
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 49 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I6010
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 50 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I6010
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 51 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I6010
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 52 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I6010
        NOP
! ---- BIT 53's SIC,SEN ends PDF p.12; its B,SERS opens p.13 ----
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 53 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I6010
        NOP
        SIC, SEN                      ! -BIT 54 OF MASK REG NOT ZERO.
        B, SERS                       ! -UNABLE TO TEST ANY FURTHER BITS.
        B, I6010
        NOP
